<protean:artefact type="html" title="Test Report">
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Test Report</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
            line-height: 1.6;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 2rem;
            color: #333;
        }
        h1 {
            color: #2c3e50;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Test Report</h1>
    <p>This is a placeholder paragraph demonstrating the basic structure of a test report. It contains sample text to illustrate how content would appear on this page. Replace this section with actual report details, findings, or analysis as needed.</p>
</body>
</html>
</protean:artefact>

Done. The page includes semantic HTML5 structure, basic styling for readability, and a responsive viewport meta tag. You can now replace the placeholder paragraph with actual report content.
